isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a72fd"}, {"id": "a4bb5a", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a72fe"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a72ff", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b78a3a78c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4775"], "concepts": ["6176f4036581241c7072bd0e"], "question": {"text": "Sugar moiety in DNA and RNA molecules respectively are"}, "options": [{"id": "9a0602", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></math>deoxyribose, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math>deoxyribose", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7300"}, {"id": "b94437", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math>ribose, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>deoxyribose", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7301"}, {"id": "a7bff4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></math>deoxyribose, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math>ribose", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7302"}, {"id": "299858", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>deoxyribose, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>deoxyribose", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7303"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7304", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b78a3a78c"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1ea2"], "concepts": ["6117b5e4478ae845c43c5e38"], "question": {"text": "What are the functional groups present in the structure of maltose?"}, "options": [{"id": "f7bd28", "text": "One ketal and one hemiketal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7305"}, {"id": "d3db8d", "text": "Two acetals", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7306"}, {"id": "770993", "text": "One acetal and one hemiacetal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7307"}, {"id": "15a39b", "text": "One acetal and one ketal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7308"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7309", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b78a3a78c"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5674"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa033"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :<br />Statement (I) : On hydrolysis, oligo peptides give rise to fewer number of $\\alpha$-amino acids while proteins give rise to a large number of $\\beta$-amino acids.<br />Statement (II) : Natural proteins are denatured by acids which convert the water soluble form of fibrous proteins to their water insoluble form.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "9d0deb", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a730a"}, {"id": "4b93da", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a730b"}, {"id": "728921", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a730c"}, {"id": "c12c61", "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a730d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a730e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b78a3a78c"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95eb"], "concepts": ["6162fc0c6ed13040ec8560b2"], "question": {"text": "Deficiency of vitamin K causes :"}, "options": [{"id": "57ef8d", "text": "Increase in blood clotting time", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a730f"}, {"id": "722347", "text": "Increase in fragility of RBC&nbsp;&#39;s", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7310"}, {"id": "1ffbbc", "text": "Cheilosis", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7311"}, {"id": "664889", "text": "Decrease in blood clotting time", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7312"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7313", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b78a3a78c"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1ea3"], "concepts": ["6117b76b478ae845c43c6d58"], "question": {"text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5YDiPPaPk6ZxeS0q9p3ZCUrU-GE96kY1yAtTt3tbc_A.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />The incorrect statements regarding enzymes are :\n(A) Enzymes are biocatalysts.\n(B) Enzymes are non-specific and can catalyse different kinds of reactions.\n(C) Most Enzymes are globular proteins.\n(D) Enzyme - oxidase catalyses the hydrolysis of maltose into glucose.\nChoose the correct answer from the option given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "48ff9b", "text": "(B), (C) and (D)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7314"}, {"id": "7d374c", "text": "(B) and (D)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7315"}, {"id": "f6aaec", "text": "(A), (B) and (C)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7316"}, {"id": "2d514d", "text": "(B) and (C)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7317"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7318", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b78a3a78c"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f43"], "concepts": ["6162fc0b6ed13040ec855fc9"], "question": {"text": "Which is not true for arginine?"}, "options": [{"id": "b8428a", "text": "It has a fairly high melting point", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a7319"}, {"id": "b2c902", "text": "It is associated with more than one <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;values.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a731a"}, {"id": "485cd3", "text": "It has high solubility in benzene.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a731b"}, {"id": "9dee6d", "text": "It is a crystalline solid.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a731c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9a2ee0e063d92a731d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b78a3a78c"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f1"], "concepts": ["60e5673a499d1e49588f8b73"], "question": {"text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> are three biomolecules. The results of the tests performed on them are given below:<table border=\"1px solid\">\t<thead>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<th>&nbsp;</th>\t\t\t<th>Molisch&#39;s test</th>\t\t\t<th>Barfoed Test</th>\t\t\t<th>Biuret Test</th>\t\t</tr>\t</thead>\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Positive</td>\t\t\t<td>Negative</td>\t\t\t<td>Negative</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Positive</td>\t\t\t<td>Positive</td>\t\t\t<td>Negative</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Negative</td>\t\t\t<td>Negative</td>\t\t\t<td>Positive</td>\